      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I guess if you're the type of person who is *that* protective of your birthday, so much so that you never.. celebrate it in VR, mention it to friends in VR, or ever bring any attention to it at all, that's fair. But that kind of person with that level of privacy concern likely doesn't want to age verify to begin with. I can't imagine the mind of a person who is worried someone will stalk their profile every day for a year when they're 17 to see the DAY it flips to 18, but also feels comfortable giving their ID to a third party company.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
